## Notes / open items
- **Debit-pay bill payment is the standout target.** Two cards confirmed to accept a **debit card** for the monthly bill: **Capital on Tap** (Payments page) and the **Venmo Credit Card** (debit card / Venmo balance / bank). All corporate charge cards (Brex, Ramp, BILL/Divvy, Rho, Mercury IO, Airbase) settle by **ACH/bank autopay only = No**. Robinhood Gold is also **ACH-only = No**. PayPal Cashback and Airbase debit-pay left NEEDS RESEARCH.
- **Best Costco combo:** **Capital on Tap** (Visa, flat 1.5–2%, debit-fundable bill) and **Robinhood Gold** (Visa, flat 3%) are the only cards that both work at Costco (Visa) and earn a meaningful flat rate there. Mastercard cards (Brex, Rho, Mercury IO, PayPal, SoFi) can't be swiped at Costco in-warehouse at all.
- **Grocery/Costco MCC:** No card here has a grocery-category bonus that clearly includes Costco except possibly the **Venmo Credit Card** (its "grocery" category reportedly includes wholesale clubs — verify per statement). Elsewhere Costco's MCC 5300 warehouse-club coding earns only flat/base rate, never a grocery multiplier.
- Fields still NEEDS RESEARCH: Airbase/Paylocity reward rate + fees + debit-pay; BILL Divvy FX fee; Rho FX fee; Mercury FX fee; Venmo Debit FX fee; PayPal FX fee & debit-pay; Cash App grocery Boost; X Money card fee.
